{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792406122,"nonce":"/d/p+DJnB2hHPviv6DwXDzrYtPg=","title":"Code inside a taken #if branch is reported one or more lines early","message":"`parser::preprocessor::preprocess` emitted the taken branch of an `#if` block first and padded blank lines only after it. Every line inside the branch therefore moved up by the lines before it in the block: the `#if` line and any branches not taken. Lines after `#end` were right again.\n\nRepro (with `-D js` or any active define):\n```haxe\nvar v = Lib.answer() + nope;\n```\n\"Cannot find name 'nope'\" was reported on the `#if js` line. Diagnostics, `trace` positions (PosInfos) and editor positions inside conditional code were all affected, and LSP lookups inside such blocks found nothing.\n\nFix: `process_conditional_block` returns one entry per line between `#if` and `#end`, with an empty line for directives and untaken lines, so each kept line stays at its source number.","files":null}]}